WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.258
When Dr. Dolittle was a people doctor, he once helped a sick sailor.

2
00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:09.957
The sailor was very grateful to the doctor.

3
00:00:09.958 --> 00:00:14.133
"I will give you whatever you want," he promised.

4
00:00:14.134 --> 00:00:17.895
So Dr. Dolittle decided to ask for his help.

5
00:00:17.896 --> 00:00:21.085
"I need to travel to Africa," he said.

6
00:00:21.086 --> 00:00:26.667
"You may use my boat," the sailor answered.

7
00:00:26.668 --> 00:00:31.489
Soon Dr. Dolittle was ready for the great journey to Africa.

8
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:35.092
He felt excited and sad at the same time.

9
00:00:35.093 --> 00:00:40.120
He could not take all the animals with him.

10
00:00:40.121 --> 00:00:44.320
"Take care of the house," he said to the remaining animals.

11
00:00:44.321 --> 00:00:47.795
"Stay warm and drink lots of water."

12
00:00:47.796 --> 00:00:55.972
"We’ll miss you, Dr. Dolittle," the animals cried.

13
00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:58.866
For six long weeks, they sailed.

14
00:00:58.867 --> 00:01:03.045
Polynesia and Chee-Chee enjoyed the sun and the ocean.

15
00:01:03.046 --> 00:01:06.405
"Can you see Africa yet?" the monkey asked.

16
00:01:06.406 --> 00:01:10.398
"Not yet, Chee-Chee, but soon," answered the doctor.

17
00:01:10.399 --> 00:01:16.590
The parrot and the monkey were so excited to return to Africa, their home.However,

18
00:01:16.591 --> 00:01:20.629
the others were not enjoying themselves too much. "Oh,

19
00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:25.299
I feel so sick," the green pig moaned. "Don’t

20
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:34.239
get sick on me!" growled Jip. "It’s

21
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:39.550
too bad you can’t swim," Dab-Dab jumped onto the boat. "The

22
00:01:39.551 --> 00:01:42.191
water is so warm today." "Hey!

23
00:01:42.192 --> 00:01:49.141
Watch it!" Too-Too did not like water at all. John

24
00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:54.682
Dolittle was a good doctor, but not a good sailor. "I’m

25
00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:58.265
afraid we’re lost," he said one morning. "Yoo-hoo!"

26
00:01:58.266 --> 00:02:00.180
"What

27
00:02:00.181 --> 00:02:04.090
was that?" asked Gub-Gub. "What

28
00:02:04.091 --> 00:02:05.264
was what? I

29
00:02:05.265 --> 00:02:08.373
didn’t hear anything!" growled Jip. "Oh,

30
00:02:08.374 --> 00:02:10.797
yoo-hoo!" "Look!

31
00:02:10.798 --> 00:02:14.748
Over there!" shouted Dab-Dab. The

32
00:02:14.749 --> 00:02:18.470
sound was coming from two dolphins. "Are

33
00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:22.484
you Dr. Dolittle?" called out one dolphin. "Yes,

34
00:02:22.485 --> 00:02:27.929
I am. How did you know?" Dr. Dolittle asked, surprised.

35
00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:30.000
"We heard all about you, Doctor.

36
00:02:30.001 --> 00:02:35.213
You’re famous!" shouted the other one.

37
00:02:35.214 --> 00:02:39.028
"We must get to Africa," said Chee-Chee.

38
00:02:39.029 --> 00:02:43.309
"We know. We’ll help you get there," said the first dolphin.

39
00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.120
"Just follow us!" said the other.

40
00:02:47.121 --> 00:02:53.586
"I bet I could swim faster than them!" Dab-Dab said with a sniff.

41
00:02:53.587 --> 00:02:58.050
The dolphins guided Dr. Dolittle’s boat across the ocean.

42
00:02:58.051 --> 00:03:03.520
As they passed by, fish and whales swam up to see the animal doctor.

43
00:03:03.521 --> 00:03:08.559
"That’s the human who speaks our language!" whispered a large fish.

44
00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.942
"He’s going to save the monkeys!" shouted the whale.

45
00:03:13.943 --> 00:03:17.699
Finally it was time for the dolphins to leave them.

46
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:21.917
"This is as far as we can go," one dolphin said.

47
00:03:21.918 --> 00:03:27.097
"Just keep going straight and you’ll see land," the other said.

48
00:03:27.098 --> 00:03:31.123
"How can we ever thank you?" asked Dr. Dolittle.

49
00:03:31.124 --> 00:03:33.677
"Save the monkeys, Doctor."

50
00:03:33.678 --> 00:03:39.455
The dolphins swam away into the sunset.

51
00:03:39.456 --> 00:03:42.352
That night, there was a terrible storm.

52
00:03:42.353 --> 00:03:45.480
The waves carried the boat in every direction.

53
00:03:45.481 --> 00:03:52.332
"Oh, I’m going to be sick," Gub-Gub, who was greener than ever, moaned.

54
00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:56.929
"Hold on tight!" shouted Jip.

55
00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:59.968
The wind howled and the sky roared.

56
00:03:59.969 --> 00:04:05.365
"Are we ever going to make it to Africa?" cried Chee-Chee.

57
00:04:05.366 --> 00:04:08.541
Suddenly the boat hit something hard.

58
00:04:08.542 --> 00:04:12.265
Water began to fill the boat.

59
00:04:12.266 --> 00:04:16.146
"Jump off! Jump off!" shouted Jip.

60
00:04:16.147 --> 00:04:21.226
"Doctor! We’re almost on land!" Too-Too pointed.

61
00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:26.556
"Quick! Dab-Dab! Take this rope!" Polynesia commanded.

62
00:04:26.557 --> 00:04:31.958
"Tie it around that tree!"

63
00:04:31.959 --> 00:04:36.956
One by one, the animals and Dr. Dolittle crossed to land.

64
00:04:36.957 --> 00:04:40.237
They watched as the water swallowed up their boat.

65
00:04:40.238 --> 00:04:45.029
"We don’t have a boat anymore," Gub-Gub said sadly.

66
00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:52.995
"But we’re alive. That’s the most important thing," Dr. Dolittle smiled.

